A few comments on that. The "few no-teleport levels" actually can be
quite significant; something like _one third_ of the Gehennom levels
are non-teleport (ignoring the Valley, Moloch's Sanctum, and Vlad it's
_seven_ levels) and given the mysterious force multiplies that number
by some factor (depending on alignment), which can make traversal of
Gehennom (i.e. on the way back) often very boring, already. WRT PW I'd
say whether you can apply that depends a lot on the class played. And
finally, my experience with teleport scrolls shows a huge variance in
my games; in some games I lack a lot of the scrolls and cannot traverse
half of Gehennom, while in other games I have spare scrolls after having
completely traversed the upper dungeon. And the force (i.e. alignment)
adds another variance factor to the scroll availability probability.
And the teleport fails many times so the scrolls are used up quickly.

It's interesting to now see a thread where the player shall be slowed
down in Gehennom; I remember discussions where the opposite had been
vigorously suggested, because of "Gehennoms boredom".

